# .docker/.env
#
# Auto-loaded by `docker compose`
# (dev via the devcontainer, or a manual `docker compose up` here).
#
# These are placeholder DEV-ONLY credentials, safe to commit. They satisfy
# the ${VAR:?...} required-variable checks in docker-compose.yml so dev
# never fails interpolation, and match the values docker-compose.dev.yml
# expects the db/cache containers to run with.
#
# For a REAL production deploy, override these with actual secrets via
# docker-compose --env-file /path/to/real/env/file

# Dockerfiles (Just Copy them to the actual env, Unless u wanna keep debuging till the apocalypse) - DO NOT FUCKING CHANGE THE VERSIONS
